[0.000, "o", "\u001b[?25l\u001b[36m\u001b[1m\u001b[H── step 2 of 7 · Start a Codex peer from a Claude session \u001b[m\u000f\u001b[36m──────────────────────────────\u001b[39m       \u001b[2m\r\n$ \u001b[m\u000f\u001b[33mcxpeer spawn codex --peer-name codex-journey-1654 --prompt 'Say READY and nothing else.' --wa\u001b[39m\u001b[3;95H\u001b[1K\u001b[33m\rit --codex-home /Users/hivamoh/.codex-alt\u001b[39m\u001b[2m\r\n  starts codex in tmux, clicks through its prompts, waits until the peer is registered (that Co\u001b[m\u000f\u001b[5;95H\u001b[1K\u001b[2m\rdex account's own hooks, queue, and login)\u001b[m\u000f\r\n  started cx-codex-cxpeer-2968 (codex) in /Users/hivamoh/funProjects/cxpeer; attach with: tmux \u001b[7;95H\u001b[1K\rattach -t cx-codex-cxpeer-2968\r\n  peer codex-journey-1654 is up (thread 01a081ad-33e1-7e60-8b83-5316a2f84055); attach with: tmu\u001b[9;95H\u001b[1K\rx attach -t cx-codex-cxpeer-2968\u001b[10;95H\u001b[1K\r  \u001b[32m\u001b[1m✓ ok\u001b[m\u000f \u001b[2m2.2 s\u001b[m\u000f\u001b[11;95H\u001b[1K\u001b[36m\u001b[1m\r\n── step 3 of 7 · Claude sees the new peer \u001b[m\u000f\u001b[36m──────────────────────────"]
[0.000, "o", "────────────────────\u001b[39m       \u001b[13;95H\u001b[1K\u001b[2m\r$ \u001b[m\u000f\u001b[33mcxpeer list\u001b[39m\u001b[2m\r\n  the same list a Claude session gets from ListAgents\u001b[m\u000f                                          \r\n  claude-journey [eb39c4]  idle  /Users/hivamoh/funProjects/cxpeer                             \u001b[32m\u001b[1m\r\n  codex-journey-1654 [4ebff6]  idle  /Users/hivamoh/funProjects/cxpeer\u001b[m\u000f                         \r\n  (8 other live sessions on this machine omitted)                                              \u001b[18;95H\u001b[1K\r  \u001b[32m\u001b[1m✓ ok\u001b[m\u000f \u001b[2m0.2 s\u001b[m\u000f\u001b[19;95H\u001b[1K\u001b[36m\u001b[1m\r\n── step 4 of 7 · A second Claude account sees it too \u001b[m\u000f\u001b[36m───────────────────────────────────\u001b[39m       \u001b[2m\r\n$ \u001b[m\u000f\u001b[33mCXPEER_CLAUDE_SESSIONS_DIR=/Users/hivamoh/.claude-alt/sessions cxpeer list\u001b[39m                   \u001b[2m\r\n  the other account's registry, read on its own; the bridge registered there as well\u001b[m\u000f           \r\n  claude-journey [eb39c4"]
[0.001, "o", "]  idle  /Users/hivamoh/funProjects/cxpeer                             \u001b[32m\u001b[1m\r\n  codex-journey-1654 [4ebff6]  idle  /Users/hivamoh/funProjects/cxpeer\u001b[m\u000f                         \u001b[25;95H\u001b[1K\r  \u001b[32m\u001b[1m✓ ok\u001b[m\u000f \u001b[2m0.2 s\u001b[m\u000f\u001b[26;95H\u001b[1K\u001b[36m\u001b[1m\r\n── step 5 of 7 · Claude gives Codex a real task \u001b[m\u000f\u001b[36m────────────────────────────────────────\u001b[39m       \u001b[35m\r\n→ \u001b[1mto codex-journey-1654: \u001b[m\u000f\u001b[35m\"List the three largest source files under cxpeer/ with their line cou\u001b[39m\u001b[29;95H\u001b[1K\u001b[35m\rnts, one line each.\"\u001b[39m\u001b[2m\r\n  auth line + message on the bridge socket, plus an idle subscription\u001b[m\u000f                          \u001b[31;95H\u001b[1K\u001b[32m\r← \u001b[1manswer \u001b[m\u000f\u001b[2m(+16.3 s)\u001b[m\u000f\u001b[32;95H\u001b[1K\r  cxpeer/bridge.py — 585 lines\u001b[33;95H\u001b[1K\r  cxpeer/doctor.py — 347 lines\u001b[34;95H\u001b[1K\r  cxpeer/client.py — 246 lines\u001b[35;95H\u001b[1K\u001b[32m\r← \u001b[1midle notice \u001b[m\u000f\u001b[2m(+16.5 s)\u001b[m\u000f\r\n  cxpeer/bridge.py — 585 lines cxpeer/doctor.py — 347 "]
[0.000, "o", "lines cxpeer/client.py — 246 lines       \u001b[37;95H\u001b[1K\r  \u001b[32m\u001b[1m✓ ok\u001b[m\u000f \u001b[2m16.5 s\u001b[m\u000f\u001b[38;95H\u001b[1K\u001b[36m\u001b[1m\r\n── step 6 of 7 · Codex reaches out on its own \u001b[m\u000f\u001b[36m──────────────────────────────────────────\u001b[39m       \u001b[35m\r\n→ \u001b[1mto codex-journey-1654: \u001b[m\u000f\u001b[35m\"Run `cxpeer send --to claude-journey \"hello from inside the Codex san\u001b[39m\u001b[41;95H\u001b[1K\u001b[35m\rdbox\"` and reply with its exit code.\"\u001b[39m\u001b[2m\r\n  Codex's sandbox blocks sockets, so its cxpeer send goes through a file outbox the bridge poll\u001b[m\u000f\u001b[43;95H\u001b[1K\u001b[2m\rs\u001b[m\u000f\u001b[44;95H\u001b[1K\u001b[32m\r← \u001b[1mfrom Codex, via cxpeer send \u001b[m\u000f\u001b[2m(+7.6 s)\u001b[m\u000f\u001b[45;95H\u001b[1K\r  hello from inside the Codex sandbox\u001b[46;95H\u001b[1K\u001b[34h\u001b[?25h\r"]
